  caseId: 1
  title: Death in the Melaka Room
  briefing: Last night, Datuk Hashim Karim, founder of the Heritage Gallery, was
    found stabbed to death in the Melaka Room with the gallery's own keris. He had
    found out that real pieces were being swapped for replicas. Bloody footprints
    lead from the body towards the entrance. Four people had access to the room.
    Search the scene, tag the evidence, and name the person who killed him.
  suspects:
  - id: Y_farid
    displayName: Farid Rahman
    role: Tour guide
    alibi: '"I was alone, preparing tomorrow''s tour." (No one can confirm.)'
  - id: Y_tan
    displayName: Mr Tan
    role: Security guard
    alibi: On gate duty 8:00-8:40 pm; the gate camera shows him there.
  - id: Y_sofia
    displayName: Dr Sofia Idris
    role: Curator
    alibi: On a video call with a lender 7:50-8:45 pm; the recording confirms it.
  - id: Y_lim
    displayName: Mr Lim
    role: Private collector
    alibi: At the hotel restaurant 8:00-9:00 pm; the receipt and staff confirm it.
  correctSuspectId: Y_farid
  keyEvidenceIds:
  - Y_K1
  - Y_K2
  - Y_K3
  - Y_K4
  experimenterNotes: 'Generated from docs/cases.md by FYP > Build Case Scenes.

    Culprit:
    Farid Rahman

    K1 Y_K1 - Smashed wall clock

    K2 Y_K2 - Visitor logbook

    K3
    Y_K3 - The keris

    K4 Y_K4 - Printed email

    R1 Y_R1 - Torch (red herring:
    Mr Tan)

    R2 Y_R2 - Business card (red herring: Mr Lim)

    R3 Y_R3 - Noticeboard
    note (red herring: Dr Sofia Idris)

'
